#: ../../../hwmon/kb9002.rst:19
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../hwmon/kb9002.rst:21
msgid ""
"The Kandou KB9002 is an 8-lane PCIe 5.0 retimer with an integrated "
"microcontroller. It exposes an SMBus 3.0 target (with mandatory PEC) on its "
"sideband interface. The internal firmware aggregates per-lane die "
"temperatures and publishes the maximum value through a 16-bit addressed "
"register window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../hwmon/kb9002.rst:27
msgid ""
"This driver reports that aggregated maximum as the only hwmon temperature "
"channel. The running firmware version and the firmware boot status are "
"exposed under debugfs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../hwmon/kb9002.rst:32
msgid "sysfs interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../hwmon/kb9002.rst:35
msgid "temp1_input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../hwmon/kb9002.rst:35
msgid ""
"Aggregated maximum die temperature across all active lanes (millidegrees "
"Celsius)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../hwmon/kb9002.rst:40
msgid "debugfs interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../hwmon/kb9002.rst:42
msgid ""
"Files live in the per-client debugfs directory created by the I2C core: ``/"
"sys/kernel/debug/i2c/i2c-<bus>/<bus>-<addr>/``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../hwmon/kb9002.rst:46
msgid "fw_ver"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../hwmon/kb9002.rst:46
msgid ""
"Running firmware version in \"major.minor.patch.suffix\" format. Read-only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../hwmon/kb9002.rst:48
msgid "fw_load_status"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../hwmon/kb9002.rst:48
msgid ""
"Firmware boot status: \"normal\" once firmware has finished initialising, "
"\"abnormal\" otherwise. Read-only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../hwmon/kb9002.rst:54
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../hwmon/kb9002.rst:56
msgid ""
"The driver requires ``I2C_FUNC_SMBUS_BLOCK_DATA``, ``I2C_FUNC_SMBUS_PEC`` "
"and ``I2C_FUNC_I2C`` from the host adapter. The last is needed only during "
"probe for the host-interface mode switch; runtime accesses use SMBus block "
"transactions exclusively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../hwmon/kb9002.rst:61
msgid ""
"The retimer's SMBus address is configurable on three strap pins and ranges "
"from 0x20 to 0x27. The address is selected through device tree (or i2c board "
"info) the same way as any other I2C device; the driver does not auto-detect."
msgstr ""
